import QtslAux.Sweep.Discrete

/-! # The `CliffCrossing` benchmark row

Machine-generated theorem file internalizing a certified reachability bound for the
`CliffCrossing` benchmark system as a Lean-checked consequence of its certificate.

The system is a Markov chain on `ℤ × ℤ` (time, height): while the time coordinate is at most `50`
and the height at most `10`, each step advances time by one and the height increases by one with
probability `1/10`, and otherwise decreases by one (staying put at height `0`); all other states
are absorbing. The certificate is the exact-rational table `tbl` (depending on both coordinates),
packaged as the supermartingale witness `V`; its bounds, barrier, and drift conditions are
verified by `norm_num`-level rational arithmetic and discharged through
`Sweep.reach_le_of_battery`.

* `sound`: starting from `(0, 0)`, the probability that the height reaches `11` within the time
  horizon (`(ω n).1 ≤ 50 ∧ 11 ≤ (ω n).2` for some `n`) is at most the certificate value at the
  initial state, stated as an exact rational;
* `sound_dec`: the same bound relaxed to the decimal bound
  `0.00000000086039230499493448903152619470166747786365027150905307677`.
-/

